WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.749
(crowd stirring)

00:00:02.749 --> 00:00:04.441
- [Man] Go, go, go, go, go, go!

00:00:04.441 --> 00:00:06.586
- [Narrator] Esports isn't just a fad;

00:00:06.586 --> 00:00:09.047
it's a massive cultural phenomenon

00:00:09.047 --> 00:00:12.257
set to take over the world with
a new generation of athletes

00:00:12.257 --> 00:00:14.146
battling in virtual worlds created

00:00:14.146 --> 00:00:17.162
using advanced computing technology.

00:00:17.162 --> 00:00:19.542
- And it takes a
supercomputer to really make

00:00:19.542 --> 00:00:23.071
this lifelike game environment exist.

00:00:23.071 --> 00:00:26.702
Textures, the hair, the effect
of wind, how water moves,

00:00:26.702 --> 00:00:29.845
all of these things are
being physically modeled

00:00:29.845 --> 00:00:32.481
at a speed that feels very real,

00:00:32.481 --> 00:00:35.070
and they're doing that with technology

00:00:35.070 --> 00:00:37.252
and they're doing that in cooperation

00:00:37.252 --> 00:00:40.419
with us at Hewlett Packard Enterprise.

00:00:41.393 --> 00:00:43.253
(keyboard keys clacking)

00:00:43.253 --> 00:00:45.050
My earliest programming experiences

00:00:45.050 --> 00:00:48.077
were literally solving
tic-tac-toe-style games

00:00:48.077 --> 00:00:50.968
on personal computers back in the '80s.

00:00:50.968 --> 00:00:53.232
(keyboard keys clacking)

00:00:53.232 --> 00:00:55.110
Now I'm building some of the world's

00:00:55.110 --> 00:00:57.521
most powerful supercomputers
to take on some of the world's

00:00:57.521 --> 00:01:01.688
most grand scientific problems
in a computational way.

00:01:04.789 --> 00:01:07.901
Supercomputers are used in all
kinds of applications today,

00:01:07.901 --> 00:01:12.696
based on this very simple idea
of modeling and simulation.

00:01:12.696 --> 00:01:14.542
When we don't understand
something physically,

00:01:14.542 --> 00:01:16.643
it helps us to build a model of it,

00:01:16.643 --> 00:01:19.226
and we do that in software now.

00:01:20.312 --> 00:01:22.285
First, we develop the
physical characteristics

00:01:22.285 --> 00:01:25.989
of the object, and then
we act on it with forces

00:01:25.989 --> 00:01:28.180
to simulate real-world phenomena.

00:01:28.180 --> 00:01:30.108
You can think of pushing on the object,

00:01:30.108 --> 00:01:32.650
and does it compress, does
it crush, how does it move,

00:01:32.650 --> 00:01:35.579
how fast, how does it interact
with its surroundings.

00:01:35.579 --> 00:01:38.043
We use them to forecast the weather.

00:01:38.043 --> 00:01:41.256
We use them to predict where
the stock market is going.

00:01:41.256 --> 00:01:44.242
We use them to design cars and airplanes.

00:01:44.242 --> 00:01:45.676
I don't think folks understand

00:01:45.676 --> 00:01:48.801
that behind all that is supercomputing.

00:01:48.801 --> 00:01:52.718
(electronic synthesizer music)

00:01:53.883 --> 00:01:56.763
Gaming technology relies
heavily on graphical processing,

00:01:56.763 --> 00:01:58.846
or GPUs, instead of CPUs.

00:02:00.373 --> 00:02:03.496
GPUs use a divide-and-conquer
approach to data.

00:02:03.496 --> 00:02:05.958
We use those same GPUs
now in supercomputing

00:02:05.958 --> 00:02:08.625
to solve mathematical equations.

00:02:10.137 --> 00:02:11.983
Fundamentally, what
this will allow us to do

00:02:11.983 --> 00:02:15.733
is build larger, more
powerful supercomputers.

00:02:18.415 --> 00:02:20.760
An individual chip today, can perform

00:02:20.760 --> 00:02:24.481
a trillion mathematical
equations per second.

00:02:24.481 --> 00:02:25.987
A trillion!

00:02:25.987 --> 00:02:29.197
There's no end to the
capabilities of the human race

00:02:29.197 --> 00:02:33.977
to make advances through
mathematical simulations.

00:02:33.977 --> 00:02:36.729
That's what excites me, to be
able to see the advancements

00:02:36.729 --> 00:02:39.510
that that 12-year-old kid
couldn't have imagined.

00:02:39.510 --> 00:02:41.631
Today, anything's possible.

00:02:41.631 --> 00:02:45.548
(electronic synthesizer music)

